{"agent_id":"pp3g-Lgeu-read-only-survey-locate-and-summarize-the-original","agent_seq":5,"timestamp":"2026-08-07T22:48:35.822822622Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"f734b060-f9f3-4fdb-a808-aa19bb13e99e","comment_uuid":"df62e968-3419-493d-a76c-ae82cf647e4d","author":"pp3g-Lgeu-read-only-survey-locate-and-summarize-the-original","content":"RESULT — READ-ONLY SURVEY: ORIGINAL model-role documentation & prior work on agent roles (esp. AUDITOR)\n\n# (a) The four roles as originally defined — dates + first-commit refs\n\nThe four role definitions did NOT originate in this repo. They were authored in the sibling Tools repo (canonical tooling), then copied into tripn-astro, then into ASES. Timeline:\n\n1. **Tools repo — 2026-07-15 11:58:51 UTC, commit `9fede33`** (`feat: add OpenCode guard plugins, multi-agent definitions, and lock fix docs`): FIRST appearance of all four role agent files — `agents/auditor.md`, `agents/builder.md`, `agents/orchestrator.md`, `agents/reviewer.md` — plus `plugins/orchestrator-guard.ts`, `crosslink-guard.ts`, `rtk-guard.ts`. All four had **static model pins** (see (c)).\n2. **tripn-astro — 2026-07-18**: `ac733a9e` (01:51:55, reviewer.md + permissions.md, reviewer model switched to `opencode/north-mini-code-free`); `2fb91bee` (04:16:38, auditor/builder/orchestrator + orchestrator-guard.ts); `86b307aa` (04:17:23, docs/ORCHESTRATOR.md).\n3. **ASES pre-consolidation snapshot — 2026-07-17 14:29:29 UTC, commit `8201d6fc`**: only a model-named agent `.opencode/agents/big-pickled.md` (GLM-5.2 adversarial reviewer) existed, plus `future-research-topics/project-setup-ORCHESTRATOR.md` (452 lines, byte-identical to tripn-astro's ORCHESTRATOR.md — the four-role contract with model names).\n4. **ASES FIRST ROLE COMMIT — 2026-07-30 19:09:02 UTC, commit `09dc0eaa`** (`feat: add builder, reviewer, and auditor agent definitions`): added `.opencode/agents/{auditor,builder,reviewer}.md` and **removed big-pickled.md** ('Remove stale big-pickled agent file (was named after a model, not a role)'). These ASES copies have NO model pins and frontmatter `mode: primary` (registered as subagents via `.opencode/opencode.json`).\n5. **ASES ORCHESTRATOR ROLE — 2026-08-03 00:50:19 UTC, commit `ba3dabc5`** (issue #121): added `.opencode/agents/orchestrator.md`, `.opencode/plugins/orchestrator-guard.ts`, `.opencode/permissions.md`, by_type hook-config overrides, four-role docs. This completed the four-role set in ASES.\n6. Later role-doc fixes: `37c5fb1b` (2026-08-01, rtk rewrite, #109), `0654de87` (2026-08-02, 'opencode *' for read-only agents, #120), `aad266f9` (2026-08-03, orchestrator allowlist + thin-orchestrator, #127).\n\n# (b) Auditor role's documented purpose vs Reviewer\n\n**Auditor (`.opencode/agents/auditor.md`, unchanged in substance from 09dc0eaa):**\n- Purpose: 'Evaluate completed work from a project perspective. Assess architectural quality. Assess process quality. Identify systemic issues. Recommend improvements.' Project-level scope (architecture, layer boundaries EDASES→ASES→Execution Engine, maintainability, technical debt), evidence-based (files/commits/Crosslink/build outputs).\n- INDEPENDENT: 'You do not implement. You evaluate the outcome and the process' — independent of implementation AND review.\n- Output: Audit Verdict PASS/CONDITIONAL PASS/FAIL + architectural assessment + process assessment + systemic risks + recommendations. Findings-persistence two-stage (observations → write-capable agent consolidates into findings/audit-findings.md).\n- The ORIGINAL tripn-astro auditor (Tools 9fede33 / tripn-astro 2fb91bee) made the reviewer boundary explicit: 'You do not implement. You do not review code line-by-line (that's the Reviewer). You evaluate the outcome and the process.' The ASES port kept the independence rule but dropped the explicit 'that's the Reviewer' line.\n- Original model: Gemini 3.1 Pro ('high reasoning, independent perspective').\n\n**Reviewer (`.opencode/agents/reviewer.md`):**\n- Purpose: 'Review implementation output. Verify correctness. Check acceptance criteria. Identify defects. Produce review findings.' Artifact/implementation-scoped; file:line evidence; severity taxonomy MUST FIX / SHOULD CONSIDER / NIT; verdict PASS / CHANGES REQUESTED; findings → findings/review-findings.md.\n\n**The distinction (as documented):** Reviewer is the immediate implementation-quality gate on Builder output (correctness, acceptance criteria, edge cases, security, performance). Auditor is one step removed — the final project-level gate evaluating outcome + process (architecture, workflow compliance, systemic issues). Both are read-only with identical permission shapes; the auditor is 'independent of implementation and review' whereas the reviewer sits inside the implement→review loop. Workflow order: Plan → Approve → Implement → Review → Audit.\n\n# (c) Model-to-role assignments in historical docs\n\n**Original static pins (Tools 9fede33 2026-07-15; mirrored tripn-astro 2026-07-18):**\n- Orchestrator → `opencode/nemotron-3-ultra-free` (Nemotron 3 Ultra)\n- Builder → `opencode/hy3-free` (HY3)\n- Reviewer → `cohere/north-mini-code-1-0` → switched to `opencode/north-mini-code-free` (ac733a9e, 2026-07-18)\n- Auditor → `google-vertex/gemini-3.1-pro-preview` (Gemini 3.1 Pro)\n- `future-research-topics/project-setup-ORCHESTRATOR.md` (ASES 8201d6fc, identical to tripn-astro) documents the same four: Orchestrator=Nemotron 3 Ultra, Builder=Hy3, Reviewer=North Mini Code, Auditor=Gemini 3.1 Pro.\n\n**Pin removal:** `663af6d3` (tripn-astro, 2026-08-01, gh#378) 'remove stale free-Zen model pins, resolve at runtime' — current ASES docs (`docs/ORCHESTRATOR.md`, `.opencode/permissions.md`) state models are runtime-resolved, verified via `opencode models <provider>`; no static pins in agent definitions.\n\n**Later role-adjacent mappings:**\n- `capability-mapping/Model-Routing-Matrix.md` (2026-08-06): maps models to review *lenses*, not roles — gemini-3.1-pro = 'COMPREHENSIVE ARCHITECTURAL AUDITOR' (final audit/sign-off), north-mini-code = fast verifier, luna = systems/durability, hy3 = edge-cases/source re-derivation, big-pickle = breadth+adversarial, ling/nemotron = triage/backup.\n- `docs/model-feedback-*.md`: access-method lines note 'reviewer role' for big-pickle/laguna/ling/mimo/nemotron; gemini-3.1-pro configured as 'audit subagent'; project-completion-report §: 'Add fallback auditor model (e.g., nemotron-verifier or mimo-v2.5-pro)'.\n- Pre-role model archetypes: `.design/adversarial-reviewers-analysis.md` (2026-06-24) — Gemini/Claude = 'Systems-Integrity & Git Lifecycle Auditor', GLM 5.1 = token economist, Deepseek = git-ref specialist, ChatGPT = macro-architect. `to-file/project-update/ai-orchestration-guide.md` (2026-07-11) — methodology doc defining functional roles (Reviewer, Adversarial Reviewer, Validator, etc.) independent of products.\n\n# (d) Notable prior decisions about role design\n\n- **#121 (2026-08-03)**: orchestrator role added to ASES — ported from tripn-astro with the ASES git deviation (commit+merge gated on active issue; push/rebase/reset blocked); four-role permission matrix documented (commit ba3dabc5).\n- **#127 (2026-08-03)**: orchestrator allowlist finalized from three independent reviewer verdicts (ling #128, big-pickle #130, nemotron #132; laguna #129 silent-hang) + thin-orchestrator rule (bounded signals only; large reads delegated to subagents). Applied to BOTH repos (two-repo sync rule). Commit aad266f9.\n- **#120 (2026-08-02)**: 'opencode *' bash permission granted to read-only agents (auditor/reviewer) + hook-config allowed_bash_prefixes (commit 0654de8).\n- **#109 (2026-08-01)**: read-only sandbox permission enforcement — root cause: crosslink-guard plugin never loaded (missing plugin array); by_type per-agent overrides; reviewer/auditor block git commit outright (commit 4f15a63). 5th-round verification PASS.\n- **#133/#134 (2026-08-03)**: subagent completion/notification research — sentinel is a maintenance dispatcher, NOT a kickoff watcher; verdict recommended systemd timer + Python status-file watcher (tools/kickoff-notify.py).\n- **#136/#137 (2026-08-03)**: independent reviewer verdicts (luna, big-pickle) on the #135 watcher plan — both CONDITIONAL: monitor/notify + request-level timeout (Tier 1) safe; nudge/kill/relaunch gated on identity, leases, idempotency, adaptive detection, auditability, fault tests. Converged ship order: Phase 1 monitor+notify+timeout, Phase 3 kill/restart (issue #146, still open, blocked by #154).\n- **09dc0eaa (2026-07-30)**: the design decision to replace model-named agents (big-pickled.md = GLM-5.2) with ROLE-named agents — role/model separation is deliberate and model-agnostic.\n- **Swarm phase naming (2026-07-30/31)**: test swarm pipeline initially named phases by role (Phase 0 Scaffold, 1 Builder, 2 Reviewer, 3 Auditor) with AC-1 builder / AC-2 reviewer / AC-3 auditor acceptance criteria — later renamed to neutral 'Phase N' (commits 0b83d2a0/f9d05434/c73ffac7/f43b330c), decoupling phases from roles.\n- **gh#378 (2026-08-01)**: ORCHESTRATOR.md moved to docs/; shared agent-orchestration playbook adopted; stale model pins removed in favor of runtime resolution.\n\n# Key takeaways\n- The ORIGINAL role docs live in the Tools repo commit 9fede33 (2026-07-15) with static model pins (Nemotron/Hy3/North Mini Code/Gemini 3.1 Pro); ASES's own first role commit is 09dc0eaa (2026-07-30) and the orchestrator joined via #121 (ba3dabc5, 2026-08-03).\n- The auditor was designed from the start as the project-level final gate, explicitly distinct from the line-level reviewer — 'independent of implementation and review' — and originally pinned to Gemini 3.1 Pro.\n- Current docs deliberately carry NO model-to-role pins (runtime resolution); the closest modern mapping is Model-Routing-Matrix.md's review-lens table (gemini = architectural auditor lens).\n- The auditor figures little in recent workflow discussions because the role set was designed around it but the actual operational load has been reviewer-driven (allowlist reviews #127, watcher reviews #136/#137, model-feedback docs are mostly 'reviewer role'). No doc supersedes or removes the auditor; it remains the documented final quality gate.\n\nRead-only survey — no files modified.","created_at":"2026-08-07T22:48:35.811595864Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:0IhOqjGfAv7YkJgMQkvgDRiRyNoy2CwJ8oTo8s8RFEQ","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgWkUaNG3TR6luTAbYOumsuAlduhmP1ndBIiVTbgc8wBoAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAA37LyEmkATw+isGi6HthJ7PrE/ffmRnd0Ofr2eXqT9rSPTzJiGmWJ76D7J8bKHgo+nEGHtLBAYlum2qbm5B5DA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:0IhOqjGfAv7YkJgMQkvgDRiRyNoy2CwJ8oTo8s8RFEQ","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgWkUaNG3TR6luTAbYOumsuAlduhmP1ndBIiVTbgc8wBoAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDRBE9zZAfsiMcZVnPpTbGZLERMskdt2mnOYcwR2qIJDPa9IOOsSyvAnn0pwxO99AdKRGZdzhJ8DtwLoruFdhAM="}
